# How many children does the average woman in the world have today?
subtitle: "Guess the world's births per woman today, take a clue and guess again, then see how it halved since the 1960s, and South Korea's record low."
tags: ["data","economics","geography"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Five kids, then…\" note \"Births per woman\""

## How many children does the average woman in the world have today?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - '1963'
      - Today
    values:
      - 5.3
      - 2.3
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 7
    y_label: Children per woman
    label_size: 36
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: 'Fertility rate: births per woman'
      authors: Our World in Data, from UN World Population Prospects (2024)
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/children-per-woman-un
      finding: world 5.31 births per woman in 1963 (the peak), 2.25 in 2023; India 1.98, China 1.0; South Korea 5.99 in 1960 and 0.72 in 2023, among the lowest of any country (Hong Kong 0.72, Macao 0.66)
    - id: owid_why
      title: The global decline of the fertility rate
      authors: Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2014
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/global-decline-fertility-rate
      finding: 'the global fertility rate has more than halved; main reasons: women''s empowerment through education and work, falling child mortality, and rising costs of raising children'
    - id: wpp
      title: World Population Prospects 2024
      authors: United Nations
      year: 2024
      finding: total fertility rate by country, 1950–2023

