    card title "How many children per woman now?"

How many children does the average woman in the world have today? In 1963, it was over five.
    draw axes bar_1

    ask "Drag the second bar to your guess for today." on bar_2 store g1 reveal false default "3.5"

Now a clue. India, the most populous country, is already below two children per woman, and China is at about one.
    draw clue

    ask "Want to change your guess? Drag the bar again." on bar_2 revise g1 store g2 default "2.6"
        right: Close: you said {g2}, and it is about {g2.true}.
        wrong: You said {g2}; it is about {g2.true}.

    erase clue

So in sixty years the world's average has more than halved, from over five children to about two point three.
    draw halved

    erase axes bar_1 bar_2 halved

Picture it: a typical mother in 1963 had five children, and then some.
    draw mom1 y63 k1_0 k1_1 k1_2 k1_3 k1_4

Today she has two, and a little bit.
    draw mom2 y23 k2_0 k2_1 k2_q parallel true

Why? Far fewer children die young, far more girls go to school and then to work, and children cost more to raise.
    highlight mom2

    erase mom1 y63 mom2 y23 k1_0 k1_1 k1_2 k1_3 k1_4 k2_0 k2_1 k2_q

One of the steepest falls anywhere came in South Korea: about six children per woman in 1960.
    draw kr krt ky60 kmom1 kk1_0 kk1_1 kk1_2 kk1_3 kk1_4 kk1_5 parallel true

In 2023: zero point seven two, among the very lowest in the world.
    draw ky23 kmom2 kk2 kv

    erase ky60 kmom1 ky23 kmom2 kk2 kv kk1_0 kk1_1 kk1_2 kk1_3 kk1_4 kk1_5

Put it another way: take ten women in South Korea today.
    draw w_0 w_1 w_2 w_3 w_4 w_5 w_6 w_7 w_8 w_9 w_l parallel true

To keep a population steady, they would need about twenty-one.
    draw o_7 o_8 o_9 o_10 o_11 o_12 o_13 o_14 o_15 o_16 o_17 o_18 o_19 o_20 o_n parallel true

They will have about seven. So each new generation there is roughly a third the size of the last.
    draw o_0 o_1 o_2 o_3 o_4 o_5 o_6 o_l parallel true

    text third "only ⅓" #b5482e x 780 y 125 font_size 64

    highlight third

